ected by Hiro  Mirai Glover's longtime music video  director and Mariah's expert visual  sense and rich use of surrealism has  made Atlanta one of the best looking  shows on television after returning to  television for the first time in 20  years in 2005 doctor who reestablished  itself as a stylish sci-fi show for a  new  audience stills despite multiple  showrunners and multiple actors playing  the eponymous doctor the next decade of  Doctor Who settled into a comfortable  rhythm an eccentric male lead on again  off again romances with various co-stars  callbacks to the original run and silly  science-fiction shenanigans joke old foe  toto  no oh so cold osso bucco Buffalo Joe  that all changed in 2018 when for the  first time a woman took over as the  title character what do we do  why are you asking her but she's in  charge bro Jesu Jodi Whitaker's turn as  the doctor ended up being exactly the  shot in the arm that the show needed  coinciding nicely with new showrunner  Chris Chibnall tenure the haunting of  Hill House is horror at its best  simultaneously terrifying and thrilling  while also dealing with the emotional  core that should be at the center of  every horror movie the richness of  character has led to some reviews  calling Hill House a drama with ghosts  or like this as us wrapped in a gothic  ghost story but make no mistake Hill  House is absolutely terrifying  director showrunner Mike Flanagan  showcases all the technical brilliance  that made oculus and Gerald's game so  profoundly scary and through it all he  never loses sight of the fact that the  ghosts are a way for the audience to  connect to the crane family's trauma  it's just that you know they're all so  scary as hell as the prequel and  sometimes kind of sequel to Breaking Bad  better call Saul takes a bit of a slower  pace than its predecessor but is still  prone to occasional explosions of  violence you're more likely to see  elaborate cons than the vicious meth  heads that populated